Debt is not a magic tax receipt

Borrowing also requires correct classification.

Government borrowing provides financing.

It does not become tax revenue simply because money arrived in the government’s bank account.

Repayment of principal reduces a liability. It is not automatically another purchase of whatever the original borrowing financed.

Interest is a financing cost and must be treated consistently within the chosen public-finance framework.

Once again, methodology has ruined an otherwise promising magic trick.

